### 
Negation / Contradiction Rules:
    ¬-Introduction: a negation ¬A may be asserted after a subproof, with A as its hypothesis containing ⊥    
    ¬-Elimination: a contradiction (⊥) may be inferred from a pair of conflicting premises A and ¬A
    
Dependencies: subproofs
###

GIVEN P IMP Q                    
GIVEN NOT Q   
DERIVE NOT P  

ASSUME P                         # push(P)
    APPLY IMP_ELIM P, P IMP Q    # yield Q
    APPLY NOT_ELIM Q, NOT Q      # yield ⊥
END                              # pop(P)

APPLY NOT_INTRO P, P             # yield ¬P 

CONCLUDE                     
